-- title:
--   Cyclicity of the torus of level automorphisms at q
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, carrying a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb{C}$ satisfies $\iota_0(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ let $K$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and let $K_0\le K$ be the analogous subfield built from $\Gamma_0(M')$-forms. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$; let $W_0\subseteq K$ and $O_0\subseteq K_0$ be the valuation subrings consisting of those $f$ with $f\cdot y=x$ for power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction. Let $\tau:\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})\to\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfy, for all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, the predicate $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}$ for $\gamma^{-1}$: under any $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau(\gamma)x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, whenever $x$ corresponds to the ratio attached to $f,g$. Finally let $H\le\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ be a subgroup each of whose elements $g$ (a) equals $\tau(\gamma)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, (b) fixes every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series lies in the $L$-base change of the $\Gamma_0(qM')$ $q$-expansion field, and (c) satisfies $g^{-1}(W_0)=W_0$, i.e. the comap of $W_0$ along $g$ is $W_0$. Then $H$ is cyclic and $\#H$ divides $q-1$.
--
--   Group-theoretically, conditions (b) and (c) pin $H$ down inside the level automorphisms of the function field of $X(\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))$ over $L$ to the intersection of the two Borel subgroups determined by the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-floor and by the stabiliser of the Gauss valuation ring at the cusp $\infty$, namely the split torus $\mathbb{F}_q^\times$ modulo $\pm 1$; the statement records the weaker divisibility $\#H\mid q-1$, which is all that is needed later. It is used in the construction of invariant finite charts with cyclic inertia at the supersingular points of $X_H$.
